diff --git a/docs/RDS_REMOVAL.md b/docs/RDS_REMOVAL.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..f644e35
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/RDS_REMOVAL.md
@@ -0,0 +1,45 @@
+# RDS removal (dev)
+
+KrishiFarms and Gamya dev no longer use managed RDS (`gamya-couture-dev-pg`). Databases run on **Docker Postgres on the shared EC2** (KrishiFarms) or **local/external Postgres** (Gamya backend).
+
+## What changed in Terraform
+
+| Setting | Value |
+|---------|-------|
+| `enable_rds` | `false` in `environments/dev/ci.tfvars` |
+| `module.rds` | `count = var.enable_rds ? 1 : 0` — destroys RDS when false |
+| `module.scheduler` | `schedule_rds = false`, `schedule_ec2 = true` |
+| `ci-backend-deploy-iam` | No `rds:StartDBInstance` when RDS disabled |
+
+Merge to `main` runs **Terraform apply** on `environments/dev` and removes:
+
+- `aws_db_instance` `gamya-couture-dev-pg`
+- DB subnet group, SSM username/password params, RDS CloudWatch log groups
+- Lambda env `DB_INSTANCE_IDENTIFIER` (scheduler EC2-only)
+
+**EC2 daily start/stop (06:00 / 11:00 IST) is unchanged.**
+
+## Apply via CI (recommended)
+
+1. Merge PR with `enable_rds = false`.
+2. Watch **Actions → Terraform** apply on `main`.
+3. Confirm plan shows **destroy** for `module.rds[0].*` resources.
+
+## Manual fallback
+
+If state is drifted or apply cannot run:
+
+```bash
+bash scripts/destroy-rds-instance.sh --dry-run
+bash scripts/destroy-rds-instance.sh
+```
+
+KrishiFarms deploy (separate repo) also runs `configure-compute-scheduler-ec2-only.sh` to drop RDS from the shared cost Lambda.
+
+## Re-enable RDS (not recommended)
+
+Set `enable_rds = true` in tfvars and apply. A **new** instance is created; data is not restored unless you import/snapshot.
+
+## Gamya application.env
+
+After RDS removal, set JDBC URL on EC2 `/opt/gamya-couture/config/application.env` to your Postgres host (local Docker, Supabase, etc.). New EC2 bootstrap uses `db_endpoint_override` (default `127.0.0.1`) when `enable_rds = false`.
